WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.012 --> 00:00:01.470
METE ATAMEL:
Translation API can be

00:00:01.470 --> 00:00:03.300
used to dynamically
translate a string

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:05.590
into any supported language.

00:00:05.590 --> 00:00:08.340
Let's see how to use
Translation API with C#.

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:10.845
First, make sure the API
is enabled in your project

00:00:10.845 --> 00:00:14.070
and the service account
exist to make API calls.

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:16.980
Both are explained in the
code lab in the video notes.

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:22.090
In Cloud Shell, let's create
a simple .NET console app.

00:00:22.090 --> 00:00:27.260
And add Translation API
NuGet package to the project.

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:31.986
Open the online code editor
and navigate to program.cs.

00:00:31.986 --> 00:00:35.010
We will translate an
English text to Turkish.

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:39.160
Reference to the
Translation API library.

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:41.440
Create translation client.

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:44.080
Specify the text to
translate, and call

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:48.520
Translate Text on the text
with to and from languages.

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:50.708
Finally, print the translation.

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:56.480
Let's run the app.

00:00:56.480 --> 00:00:57.140
There you go.

00:00:57.140 --> 00:01:00.640
You just translated text
using Translation API.

